    "narrative": "For LawDog today, our most productive offensive engine will likely be **Luis Arraez** (69.53) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02). **Luis Arraez** benefits significantly from the lead-off spot against Civale, and despite a lukewarm BvP history, the +10% order bonus and favorable wind conditions elevate his profile. **Jung Hoo Lee** also gains major utility from the wind out at the park and a massive +19% bump in SP skill favorability, making him a cornerstone play. **Cal Raleigh** (66.95) also presents a strong floor, as the combination of his #2 spot in the order and wind-aided hitting environment offsets the minor platoon disadvantage against Keller.\n\nThe rotation decision regarding **Geraldo Perdomo** (56.21) proved the most difficult bench choice of the session. While his #2 batting order position usually demands a starting spot, the extreme depth of our current lineup\u2014particularly the high-efficiency matchup for **Daulton Varsho** (63.68) and **Gavin Sheets** (62.01)\u2014pushed him to the pine. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Taylor Ward**; should either fall out of the top third of the order, their efficiency scores will crater, necessitating a shift to our bench depth. Notably, **Yainer Diaz** (48.97) remains our most volatile start of the day due to the difficult matchup against Bieber; he is hovering near our marginal threshold and will be the first candidate pulled if mid-game conditions sour.",
